  "full_response": "Creating a comprehensive comparison of all major cloud providers—Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform (GCP)—across various service categories involves examining several aspects like pricing, service offerings, ease of use, global reach, integrations, and more. Below is a broad comparison including 20 different service categories:\n\n### 1. Compute Services\n\n- **AWS**: \n  - **Pros**: Offers EC2 with a variety of instance types; strong integration with other AWS services; mature and broad feature set.\n  - **Cons**: Complex pricing structure; can be overwhelming for new users.\n- **Azure**:\n  - **Pros**: Good integration with Microsoft products; Virtual Machine Scale Sets for automated and secure scaling.\n  - **Cons**: Newer in the market than AWS, though catching up quickly.\n- **GCP**:\n  - **Pros**: Excellent for containerized applications using Kubernetes; sustained use discounts.\n  - **Cons**: Fewer features and options compared to AWS.\n\n### 2. Storage Services\n\n- **AWS**: \n  - **Pros**: Wide range of storage options (S3, EBS, Glacier); highly reliable and secure.\n  - **Cons**: Pricing can be complex and sometimes expensive.\n- **Azure**: \n  - **Pros**: Strong integration with other Microsoft services; Blobs, Files, and Disks.\n  - **Cons**: Pricing can be complex.\n- **GCP**: \n  - **Pros**: Cost-effective; supports object, block, and file storage.\n  - **Cons**: Fewer features than AWS.\n\n### 3. Database Services\n\n- **AWS**: \n  - **Pros**: Managed services like RDS, DynamoDB, Aurora; broad database support.\n  - **Cons**: Can be expensive for large-scale deployments.\n- **Azure**:\n  - **Pros**: Azure SQL, Cosmos DB; strong for hybrid cloud scenarios.\n  - **Cons**: Newer databases might not be as mature.\n- **GCP**: \n  - **Pros**: Excellent for NoSQL with Firestore and Bigtable; strong analytics with BigQuery.\n  - **Cons**: Limits on database sizing and options.\n\n### 4. Networking\n\n- **AWS**: \n  - **Pros**: VPC for private subnets; route tables and VPN support.\n  - **Cons**: Can be complex to configure.\n- **Azure**:\n  - **Pros**: Virtual Network; strong regional presence.\n  - **Cons**: Interface can be less intuitive.\n-",
